Why This Is Asked
Tests practical error handling and DLQ routing in KCNA pipelines, a common real-world requirement. Emphasizes per-topic isolation, backpressure, and safe offset management.

Key Concepts
- Dead-letter routing per topic
- Retry policy with backoff and max attempts
- Offset commits tied to successful processing
- Canary validation of DLQ behavior and downstream progress

Code Example
```javascript
function onMessage(msg) {
  try {
    const payload = parse(msg.value);
    if (!isValid(payload)) throw new Error('invalid payload');
    process(payload);
    commitOffsets(msg); // on success
  } catch (e) {
    routeToDL(msg, e.message); // to sensor_DL or alerts_DL based on topic
  }
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor DLQ growth and set alert thresholds?
- What strategies prevent DLQ messages from growing unbounded while ensuring no data loss in the main path?
